===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|nl|veugel||obsolete}}
* {{alt|nl|fogel}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|nl|dum|vōgel}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|fogal}}, {{m|odt|vogal}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*fugl}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*fuglaz}}. Cognate with {{cog|de|Vogel}}, {{cog|en|fowl}}, {{cog|is|fugl}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/ˈvoːɣəl/|q2=Hollandic|[ˈfoʊ̯χɔɫ]}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-vogel.ogg}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|vo|gel}}
* {{rhyme|nl|oːɣəl|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{nl-noun|m|-s|pl2=-@en|+|dim2=-ijn}}

# {{C|nl|Vertebrates}} [[bird]], any member of the class [[Aves]]
#: {{ux|nl|De tuin zit vol met verschillende soorten '''vogels''', zoals merels, mussen en roodborstjes.|The garden is full of different types of '''birds''', such as blackbirds, sparrows, and robins.}}
#: {{ux|nl|Het geluid van fluitende '''vogels''' vulde de lucht in de vroege ochtend.|The sound of chirping '''birds''' filled the air in the early morning.}}
# a [[feathered]] target in [[archery]] or [[shooting]]
#: {{syn|nl|gaai}}
#: {{ux|nl|De schutter mikte op het kleine '''vogeltje''' dat op de paal was geplaatst.|The archer aimed at the small '''feathered target''' placed on the pole.}}
#: {{ux|nl|Het schieten op '''vogels''' is een traditionele sport in sommige landen.|Shooting at '''bird''' targets is a traditional sport in some countries.}}
# {{lb|nl|figuratively||slang}} a [[dude]], a [[cat]] {{gloss|slang term for a man}}

====Usage notes====
The word ''vogel'' is one of the few words where the obsolete Dutch diminutive suffix {{m|nl|-lijn}} can still be encountered: {{m|nl|vogelijn||little bird}} is chiefly poetic and can be found in poems and songs, but is not often used elsewhere.

